  "metadata": {
    "title": "Energy burden vs income and solution savings \u2014 Cuba, NM (Census Tract 109, Sandoval County)",
    "created": "2026-10-27",
    "energy_burden_definition": "Annual home energy cost / annual household income x 100",
    "high_burden_threshold_pct": 6.0,
    "data_caveats": [
      "Primary data is DOE LEAD for Census Tract 109, Sandoval County (820 households, the Cuba area). Statewide LEAD kept for comparison.",
      "LEAD burden percentages are rounded to whole numbers; computed_burden_pct uses cost/income directly.",
      "Statewide electric vs heating split is estimated from LEAD component burdens.",
      "Cuba heating costs are eRedux modeled values for a ~2,000 sq ft home; real Cuba homes may be smaller.",
      "Eligibility uses a household size of 3 (Cuba avg 3.07). Solar for All eligibility for Cuba scenarios uses the SNAP/LIHEAP route because Sandoval 80% AMI was not verified.",
      "Wood-heat scenarios exclude firewood cost (no reliable local figure), so they understate burden."
    ]
  },
